      "id": 1,
      "text": "Williamstown was founded in 1826 by Daniel Williams, after whom the borough is named.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.williamstownborough.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Coal mining began in 1866, and by 1873 Williamstown was the largest anthracite colliery in the world.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.williamstownborough.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The borough celebrated its 200th anniversary in 2026, spotlighting its coal heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://wynninghistory.com/2025/12/31/williamstown-article-200th/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Williamstown sits in the valley of Wiconisco Creek, flanked by Big Lick Mountain to the north and Berry Mountain to the south.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Williamstown%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Route 209 skirts the south of the borough, linking it to Pottsville and Elizabethville.",
